1
00:00:28,146 --> 00:00:34,957
I hold his arm beside the door,
His anger leaves him more and more.

2
00:00:35,046 --> 00:00:41,802
"Please watch my boy, please take good care,
His music and his love are there."

3
00:00:41,913 --> 00:00:48,457
I want to scream, I want to cry!
I watch my precious young son die!

4
00:00:48,743 --> 00:00:56,387
I choose the peace, I hide the truth,
And choke the freedom of his youth!

5
00:01:09,294 --> 00:01:16,183
I walk into the room again,
My husband sitting silent then.

6
00:01:16,319 --> 00:01:22,952
He called her 'that girl' with a sneer,
And mocked the one he holds so dear.

7
00:01:23,078 --> 00:01:29,722
I want to scream, I want to cry!
I watch my precious young son die!

8
00:01:29,832 --> 00:01:38,199
I choose the peace, I hide the truth,
And choke the freedom of his youth

9
00:01:50,470 --> 00:01:57,359
You chose me too when we were young,
Despite the heavy bitter tongue.

10
00:01:57,448 --> 00:02:04,214
Why can't you let him have his heart?
Why tear his living soul apart?

11
00:02:04,224 --> 00:02:10,924
I want to scream, I want to cry!
I watch my precious young son die!

12
00:02:11,041 --> 00:02:18,586
I choose the peace, I hide the truth,
And choke the freedom of his youth!

13
00:02:31,684 --> 00:02:38,540
He lies upstairs upon his bed,
With heavy thoughts inside his head.

14
00:02:38,629 --> 00:02:45,195
The red accordion stays cold,
With dust upon its keys of gold.

15
00:02:45,329 --> 00:02:52,129
I want to scream, I want to cry!
I watch my precious young son die!

16
00:02:52,227 --> 00:03:01,060
I choose the peace, I hide the truth,
And choke the freedom of his youth!

17
00:03:12,703 --> 00:03:19,458
"I miss her, mom, I cannot sleep,"
His quiet words I deeply keep.

18
00:03:19,703 --> 00:03:26,392
I taught him how to speak and love,
While silent skies look down above...

19
00:03:26,481 --> 00:03:33,303
The music dies inside his soul,
While dark shadows take control.

20
00:03:33,455 --> 00:03:44,733
I hold my hands, I stay in place...
And weep for his lost, sweet embrace.

